  "editorial_article": "Formed in 2010 by Big Hit Entertainment CEO Bang Si-hyuk in Seoul, BTS debuted in 2013 with the single album 2 Cool 4 Skool. The group initially utilized a 1990s old-school hip-hop sound on tracks like 'No More Dream' and 'N.O.', which addressed student anxiety and societal pressures in South Korea. Members RM, Suga, and J-Hope provided the group's early creative core, eventually expanding their style to incorporate pop, R&B, and EDM. Their 2018 album Love Yourself: Tear reached number one on the Billboard 200, the first K-pop album to do so. In 2020, their English-language single 'Dynamite' hit number one on the Billboard Hot 100, marking their status as a global pop force. The group has historically addressed themes of self-love, mental health, and philosophy, including a conceptual alternate universe storyline woven through their discography.",
